      {
        "id": 215942,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-04T11:55:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/speedyolrac\">@speedyolrac</a>, <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/jffdougan\">@jffdougan</a>: It's more that I have to admit it's still hard to swallow spending $80 on something only I'll get to use…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Spirit Island is a super-fun game to play solo. It's by far my favorite solo game. The players at the One-Player Guild on BoardGameGeek are also incredibly enthusiastic about it. If that possibility appeals to you, I'd encourage you to try it out. (And you should be able to get it for well less than $80, once the reprint comes in.)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The last time I played, during setup I was trying to lift a Sentinels playmat to retrieve a character card that had inexplicably decided to disappear under it when I tried to set the card down and in the process I managed to accidentally throw the entire table and its contents across the room instead and so decided I was going to shelve the program entirely for now and move onto other vidya games for a while.<br>\nI have no experience with TTS, but the image of flipping the table in a virtual game is just too good.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:47:30.442Z",
